WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.616
Moving a tensor must not erase the object around it.
Transformers five point twenty point two fixes this
generation bug.

00:00:11.836 --> 00:00:19.111
The old helper kept tensor values, but changed a model
output into a plain dictionary. Attribute access then
failed.

00:00:19.331 --> 00:00:25.773
We tested two tiny models with random weights. Both
worked on the normal CPU path in both versions.

00:00:25.993 --> 00:00:31.711
When we forced the transfer branch, both failed before
the patch. Both generated tokens after it.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:38.331
The patch rebuilds a dictionary with its original
class. That preserves model outputs and their nested
fields.

00:00:38.551 --> 00:00:44.183
But it is not a universal adapter. A default dictionary
still failed our separate boundary check.

00:00:44.403 --> 00:00:49.885
Check values, shapes, and object types. Test the
transfer path as well as the normal path.

00:00:50.105 --> 00:00:55.140
These are CPU regression checks, not a GPU test or a
model quality score.
